-title><invention-title load-source="docdb" status="new" lang="FR">PROCEDE DE TRANSMISSION DIRECTIVE ET DISPOSITIF DE COMMUNICATION A COMMANDE DE DIRECTIVITE</invention-title><citations><patent-citations><patcit ucid="JP-10117162-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>10117162</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-10276124-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>10276124</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="YP" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit><patcit ucid="JP-6197059-A" status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>6197059</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id> <sources><source category="Y"  name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit> <patcit ucid="JP-9074375-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9074375</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9219675-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9219675</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIRAMATSU KATSUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IDE MINAKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC IND CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRAMATSU, KATSUHIKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IDE, MINAKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC INDUSTRIAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIRAMATSU KATSUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IDE MINAKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRAMATSU, KATSUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IDE, MINAKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method is provided for adaptively controlling transmission directivity. Radio waves arriving via two or more paths are received, and the signals are demodulated for individual paths. The demodulated signals are compared in level or quality with one another, the highest or best one is selected, and the path corresponding to the selected signal is used for transmission. If some of the signals arriving via different paths and demodulated are identical in level or quality, the history of transmission power control command (TPC) sent from the other end of communication is referred to, that is, the receiving conditions at the other end are checked. This decides whether the selected path is appropriate for transmission.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé permettant de commander de manière adaptative la directivité de transmission. Les ondes radio arrivant par deux ou plusieurs trajectoires sont reçues, et les signaux sont démodulés pour des trajectoires individuelles. Les signaux démodulés sont comparés entre eux en niveau ou en qualité. Le signal le plus élevé ou le meilleur signal est sélectionné, et la trajectoire correspondant au signal sélectionné est utilisée pour la transmission. Lorsque certains signaux arrivant par des trajectoires différentes sont démodulés et présentent un niveau de qualité identique, on se réfère à l'historique de la commande de puissance de transmission envoyée à partir de l'autre extrémité de la communication. En d'autres termes, les conditions de réception à l'autre extrémité sont vérifiées, ce qui détermine si la trajectoire sélectionnée est appropriée pour la transmission.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>